.TH CS2BLOCKCTL 1 "2026-11-08" "cs2blocker 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cs2blockctl \- manage CS2 SDR datacenter blocking rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cs2blockctl
[\fB\-\-sudo\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cs2blockctl
lists CS2 SDR POPs, selects datacenters, and applies host firewall rules.
Privileged changes are performed by a small helper through
.BR pkexec (1)
and a polkit action, or through
.BR sudo (8)
with \fB\-\-sudo\fR.
.PP
The tool only manages one nftables table,
.IR "inet cs2blocker" .
It does not touch the game, Steam, or other firewall tables.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list [\-\-region REGION] [\-\-json]
List POPs, regions, relay counts and port ranges.
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Show active rules, selection, cache freshness and boot persistence.
.TP
.B block POP...
Add POPs to the selection and switch to block mode.
.TP
.B unblock POP...
Remove POPs from the selection.
.TP
.B only POP...
Allow only the listed POPs; every other known POP is blocked.
.TP
.B preset [NAME] [\-\-list] [\-\-save] [\-\-delete]
Apply or manage presets.
.TP
.B refresh
Fetch a fresh SDR relay list and re-apply.
.TP
.B apply
Re-apply the saved selection.
.TP
.B clear
Remove all rules and empty the saved selection.
.TP
.B ping [POP...] [\-\-region REGION]
ICMP-ping relay addresses (unprivileged).
.TP
.B counters [\-\-watch]
Show live per-POP drop counters.
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-json]
Run diagnostic checks.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cs2blocker/config.json
Root-owned selection and presets, written only by the helper.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cs2blocker/sdr-730.json
Root-owned cached SDR relay list.
.TP
.I /run/cs2blocker/status.json
Live counters published by the monitor service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nft (8),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
